# =============================================================================
# @greatsales/db — Prisma CLI environment  (copy to `packages/db/.env`)
# =============================================================================
# This file is for the Prisma CLI ONLY — `prisma migrate`, `prisma studio`,
# `prisma generate`, and the seed scripts. The running API never reads it.
#
# WHY IT IS SEPARATE, AND WHY THAT MATTERS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Schema changes need the table OWNER. Serving requests must NOT use the owner,
# because an owner/superuser connection silently bypasses every Row-Level
# Security policy — the multi-tenant boundary disappears and no error is
# raised. So the project keeps two roles and never mixes them:
#
#   greatsales      OWNER    migrations, seeds, prisma studio   (this file)
#   greatsales_app  RUNTIME  the API, RLS-bound, NOBYPASSRLS    (apps/api/.env)
#
# Prisma auto-loads THIS file at require time. Because dotenv never overrides
# an already-set variable, if Prisma loads before the API's own env, the OWNER
# url would win and the API would run with RLS off. That is exactly what
# apps/api/src/load-env.ts exists to prevent — it loads apps/api/.env with
# override:true first. Do not reorder those imports.
#
# Defence in depth, in order:
#   1. this split                    (configuration)
#   2. load-env.ts import order      (process startup)
#   3. PrismaService.onModuleInit    (live connection: refuses to boot as a
#                                     superuser or a BYPASSRLS role)
#   4. explicit tenantId filters in every query
#
# Values below are for the local Docker stack (docker-compose.yml, port 5433).
# =============================================================================

# OWNER connection — DDL, migrations, seeds.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://greatsales:greatsales@localhost:5433/greatsales?schema=public"

# Prisma's `directUrl`. Same owner role; kept explicit so a pooled DATABASE_URL
# (RDS Proxy / PgBouncer) can be introduced later without breaking migrations,
# which must not run through a transaction pooler.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://greatsales:greatsales@localhost:5433/greatsales?schema=public"
